// Flat merge of the salam/llvm port (see salam/PORTING.md "Layout - FLAT"):
// compiler/src/llvm/ - one package `llvm`, one file. Import alias for
// consumers: `lv`. The backend's expr/stmt emitters are mutually recursive
// with everything else, so the module is ported by three sequential agents
// INTO THIS ONE FILE:
//
//   A (DONE): codegen_llvm_internal.h (ll_t state + inline helpers),
//       codegen_llvm_emit.c (emit context, string constants, locals),
//       codegen_llvm_type.c (LLVM type strings, layouts, symbol lookups,
//       conversions), codegen_llvm_decl.c (struct types, mangling,
//       function/lambda frames, vtables, variant boxing, globals, externs,
//       package touch), codegen_llvm.c (datalayout/prologue/on-demand
//       runtime helpers/toplevel/run), PLUS two slices other stages must
//       NOT re-port: ll_emit_defers + ll_emit_return from
//       codegen_llvm_stmt.c (the function frame needs them) and ALL of
//       codegen_llvm_debug.c (run/function frames call the DI hooks).
//   B (DONE): codegen_llvm_expr.c and the REST of codegen_llvm_stmt.c
//       (ll_stmt/ll_block/ll_block_top and every static in both files:
//       ll_binary, ll_addr_of, ll_index_set, ll_match_arm_cond, ll_call*,
//       ll_lower_print, ll_literal, ll_struct_lit, ...). Replace the three
//       stubs at the marked insertion banner IN PLACE (lv_expr,
//       lv_block_top, lv_stmt) and add the remaining functions as new
//       privates in the same section. Do NOT re-port emit_defers,
//       emit_return, emit_lambda, box_dyn/box_variant/unwrap_variant,
//       conv/as_i1/common_ts, pick_overload, strconst, local_* - stage A
//       owns them.
//   C (DONE): native toolchain glue, replacing the NativeAvailable/NativeRun
//       stubs. CORRECTION (2026-08): this banner previously claimed
//       llvm_native.c's `#ifdef SALAM_HAVE_LLVM` body was "unreachable in
//       every build this repo ships" - false. CI's flagship release builds
//       (see .github/workflows/compiler-release.yml) build the C compiler
//       with WITH_LLVM=1 WITH_LLD=1 LLVM_LINK_STATIC=1, statically linking
//       real LLVM-C + in-process LLD; only the default/dev build omits it.
//       That surface (~48 LLVM-C functions incl. the full ORC/LLJIT API,
//       plus native_link_elf/native_link_mingw's in-process LLD linking) IS
//       now ported, as its own reusable package: std/llvm/ (9 files -
//       core/target/passes/emit/orc/lld/linker + the llvm.salam/run.salam
//       entry points), not inline here, so any Salam program can drive
//       static LLVM/LLD, not just this compiler. It is deliberately NOT
//       imported by NativeRun below yet: doing so would add std/llvm's
//       `link static "LLVM"`/`link static "lldELF"`/etc directives to every
//       self-host build unconditionally (condcomp.salam's flag set is a fixed list of
//       20 OS/arch bools - there is no user-definable flag to gate an
//       opt-in the way the C's WITH_LLVM does), which would break any build
//       or CI job where those static libraries aren't installed. Wiring
//       NativeRun to prefer std/llvm when linked in - and adding whatever
//       condcomp/build-flag mechanism makes that opt-in safe - is future
//       work alongside the self-host static-link build pipeline itself
//       (std/llvm/llvm.salam has its own TODO(build-pipeline) marker).
//       Meanwhile NativeRun below still ports `salam_llvm_toolchain` - the
//       always-available fallback that shells out to `clang`/`opt`/`lli`
//       directly on the .ll text via a generated bash script (its
//       LLVM_OUT_EXEC case IS the observed `clang *.ll -lm -o <exe>`
//       convention, and its LLVM_OUT_ASM/OBJ/BITCODE/JIT/IR cases are
//       ported too). So NativeRun ports `salam_llvm_toolchain` +
//       `emit_tool_cmd` (private `nt_*` helpers below), and NativeAvailable
//       becomes a real "is a clang toolchain reachable" probe (bundled
//       tool via sm.FindBundledTool, else a PATH `--version` check) instead
//       of the C's compile-time `#ifdef` - matching what NativeAvailable is
//       actually FOR in this port (gating whether NativeRun can do
//       anything). A new pub `NativeBuildScript(ll_path, opts): str` exposes
//       the generated script text so llvm_test.salam can assert the exact
//       command line NativeRun would run without requiring a real
//       toolchain. `nt_to_tool_path`'s Windows branch (drive-letter ->
//       `/mnt/x` for `wsl.exe -e bash`) skips the C's `_fullpath`
//       resolve-to-absolute step (no equivalent Salam stdlib call) - a
//       relative path is passed through unresolved; harmless here since
//       every caller in this port already supplies a resolved-enough path
//       and the branch is compile-time-pruned out entirely on the
//       Linux/WSL builds this port is verified against (SALAM_OS_WINDOWS
//       false), same as `target_is_windows_of`'s pre-existing host-OS
//       fallback a few hundred lines up. llvm_native.c's own
//       `native_link_elf`/`native_link_mingw` in-process-lld path is now
//       ported too, as std/llvm/linker.salam's LinkElf/LinkMingw/LinkAuto -
//       see the CORRECTION above; lld_link.cc itself stays exactly as-is
//       (unported, unmodified), since it's already the minimal C-ABI shim
//       over LLD's C++ driver headers that std/llvm/lld.salam's `extern:`
//       declarations bind straight to.
//
// C -> Salam decisions for this module (B/C must inherit these):
// - ll_t -> `pub struct Lv` (all fields pub - E017). sema_result_t *sem is
//   NOT stored: thread `s &: sm.Sema` and `a &: at.Ast` through every
//   function that needs them; parameter order is (v, s, a, ...), exactly
//   like the codegen port's (g, s, a, ...).
// - arena_t* and ll_fmt(...) are GONE: strings are values; call sites build
//   text with `+` / co.I64Toa / co.U64Toa. NO co.Format in this module - //   IR text must be byte-exact, so everything is explicit concatenation.
// - "" is the C NULL for every str field/return (ts, ret_ts, this_ref,
//   self_ts, cur_sp, cur_dbg, first_error, triple, env_ref, ...); 0 is the
//   C NULL for every id (NodeId/SymId/SigId/ScopeId); local_find /
//   global_find return an INDEX into v.locals / v.globals, -1 = C NULL.
// - sb_t *g/b/allocas/hg/meta -> five str.StringBuilder fields bg (module
//   text), bb (current function body), ba (current allocas), bhg
//   (on-demand helpers), bmeta (debug metadata). The C pointer swap
//   `ll->b = &body` becomes: in_fn=true selects bb for out_b()/emit();
//   emit_function/emit_lambda SAVE the builder HEADERS (StringBuilder is a
//   {data,len,cap} value), install fresh builders, and restore after
//   appending header+entry+allocas+body to bg - byte-identical nesting
//   (inner ensure_fn'd functions land in bg before their caller, like C).
//   NEVER alias two live builders; only header save/restore is safe.
// - Value numbering: v.tmp -> "%t<N>" (new_tmp), v.lbl -> "L<N>_<tag>"
//   (new_lbl), both reset to 0 per function/lambda and saved/restored
//   around nested emission. conv() allocates its tmp AT THE SAME POINT the
//   C does (after the dyn-box check, before the int/int fast path), so
//   numbering matches even when the tmp goes unused.
// - String constants: v.strings is a Vector<LvStr> {bytes,len,hash,gref};
//   dedup by FNV-1 hash (the C's exact constants, incl. the truncated
//   0x14650FB0739D0383 offset basis) + length + bytes; gref = "@.str.<i>".
// - const char *brk[64]/cont[64] -> Vector<str> brk/cont + nloop. B's loop
//   protocol: on loop entry, if v.brk.len() == v.nloop push, else set
//   (v.nloop indexes; slots are reused exactly like the C array); the
//   64-deep clamp ("loop nesting too deep") stays.
// - bool hneed[LL_H_COUNT] -> Vector<bool> seeded by new_lv0(); the
//   LL_HELPER_EMIT function-pointer table is an if/else chain in need().
// - ll_t.ok/first_error replace the C error protocol unchanged; lv_error
//   clamps the message at 255 bytes (the C's vsnprintf buf[256]).
// - Host-dependent defaults (ll_datalayout(NULL), ll_target_ptr_bits(NULL),
//   ll_target_is_windows(NULL)) use compile-time SALAM_ARCH_*/SALAM_OS_*
//   conditionals mirroring the C's #if chains.
// - codegen_llvm.h's codegen_llvm_options_t -> pub struct Options
//   (OptionsDefault() = codegen_llvm_options_default; the C NULL opts ==
//   OptionsDefault()). llvm_output_t -> pub struct Output (field `module`
//   -> module_name like the codegen port; `error` keeps its name).
//   link_libs/link_kinds (const char *const * + nlink) -> Vector<str> x2 +
//   nlink, consumed by stage C.
// - salam_module_single_threaded comes from the codegen port
//   (cg.ModuleSingleThreaded), mirroring the C #include "codegen/codegen.h".
//
// Named `llvmgen`, in both package AND filename, to coexist with std/llvm.
// Two separate clashes had to be resolved before NativeRun could import it:
//
//  - Package: std/llvm is also `package llvm`, and two packages cannot
//    share a name - sema binds both to one symbol, so whichever loses is
//    silently unreachable ("package function 'LldAvailable' not found").
//  - Filename: a .salam file's generated C module is keyed by *filename*,
//    not package, so `compiler/llvm.salam` and `std/llvm/llvm.salam` both
//    produced salam_mod_llvm.c and silently clobbered each other, leaving
//    this module's types undeclared at their use sites ("unknown type
//    size" from tcc, in a translation unit that had never seen the struct).
//
// Every importer aliases this module (`import lv "llvmgen.salam"`), so both
// names are internal and renaming them costs nothing.
package llvmgen

import str
import co "../sal_core.salam"
import tok "../token.salam"
import at "../ast.salam"
import lg "../logger.salam"
import sm "../semantic/semantic.salam"

